## v3.0.0 (2026-08-07)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus exact-head operator merge-authorization design.
**Verification:** unverified.

### What changed

- Replaced label-only merge authority with four independent gates: automated eligibility,
  process-local reviewed-head proof, durable human exact-head authorization, and repository
  readiness.
- Added a canonical marked native `APPROVED` review, trusted-human provenance, edit and replay
  rejection, deterministic mixed-candidate precedence, and durable same-head restart recovery.
- Added bounded stable GraphQL traversal, collaborator-permission reads, immutable authorization
  capabilities, initial/final identity comparison, and fail-closed stage outcomes.
- Reconciled obsolete native auto-merge issue wording with the live SHA-conditional merge mutation
  while preserving the ban on native auto-merge mutation.
- Documented the residual dismissal race, fail-closed rollout, in-flight PR behavior, superseding
  ADR requirement, and manual branch-protected rollback.

### Why

The previous workflow made the automation-owned implementation-GO label the sole durable merge
authority. The new requirement demands one explicit human approval for the exact PR head before the
queue performs its irreversible merge mutation. GitHub's native review record supplies durable
identity and head binding, while a capability-bearing adapter boundary makes the new authorization
mechanically mandatory at the live conditional-merge call.

