## v2.4.0 (2026-08-05)

**Changed by:** ProjectHephaestus issue #2377 / PR #2657 automation-loop review and merge audit.
**Verification:** verified-ci.

### What changed

- Recorded the initial NOGO caused by an incomplete subprocess exception boundary.
- Recorded the head-bound remediation reply, exact-head/thread-snapshot handoff, exclusive NOGO→GO transition, required-check evidence, and conditional merge.

### Why

PR #2657 showed that a validator can be correctly fail-closed for returned tool failures while still leaking timeout and process-launch exceptions around the subprocess call. The review kept the PR at NOGO until those exceptions were normalized into the structured error contract and covered in both human and JSON CLI modes. The final head was then reviewed and merged through the loop-owned GO and SHA-conditional merge path.

